  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Which of the following are stochastic vectors?\n\n$$\nu=[\\begin{aligned}-0.2 \\\\ 0.7 \\\\ 0.5\\end{aligned}],\\,v=[\\begin{aligned}0.6 \\\\ -0.1 \\\\ 0.5\\end{aligned}],\\,w=[\\begin{aligned}0.15 \\\\ 0.95\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that a stochastic vector is a vector with nonnegative entries that add up to $1.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our vectors in turn.\n\n- Vector $u$ is *not* a stochastic vector since it contains negative entries.\n\n- Vector $v$ is *not* a stochastic vector since it contains negative entries.\n\n- Vector $w$is *not* a stochastic vector since the entries do not add up to one:\n\n$$\n0.15+0.95=1.1\\ne 1\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\"",
